Vendored from https://github.com/thesysdev/openui, packages/lang-core/src
Upstream commit: 9d73d17d2bbac565672a85e78f6eb7740cb0d9ca

Files (same relative paths as upstream src/): library.ts, signature.ts, reactive.ts, extend.ts,
functions.ts, parser/{ast,builtins,expressions,lexer,materialize,parser,prompt,serialize,statements,
tokens,types,validation}.ts

Relay changes, kept minimal so an upstream sync stays a plain diff:
- Every file starts with a two-line header: `// @ts-nocheck` (upstream type-checks under its own,
  looser tsconfig; Relay's stricter flags would otherwise flag upstream style) and the source path.
- Removed: telemetry (parser.ts parse wrapper, prompt.ts), OpenUI Cloud (prompt.ts cloud mode,
  parser/cloud-config.ts, parser/validate-library.ts), parser/merge.ts, parser/enrich-errors.ts,
  the parser/index.ts barrel, the runtime's query/mutation/MCP/tool-provider/state-field/
  evaluate-tree/evaluate-prop modules, message.ts, utils/, postinstall and the ci-info dependency.
- runtime/store.ts: verbatim. runtime/evaluator.ts: local state only. Library functions, custom
  actions, @Run, reactive schemas and ReactiveAssign are removed; a catalog component inside an
  expression evaluates to an ElementNode whose props stay AST (Relay's converter evaluates them);
  non-AST values (materialized elements inside expressions) pass through unchanged.
- prompt.ts: generateSystemPrompt keeps only the `{ library, promptOptions }` form.
- extend.ts: a local `mergeDefs` replaces `z.util.mergeDefs`, which zod 3.25's `zod/v4/core` lacks.
No file imports Node or DOM APIs, nothing touches the network, and nothing evaluates code
(no `eval`, no `Function` constructor).

